    <div class="itdgl-evidence-band">
      <strong>ITD CLINIC MARKETING &mdash; WHAT WE ACTUALLY DO:</strong>
      ITD GrowthLabs runs full-stack digital marketing for hair transplant + fue + fut clinics across Thane, Mumbai, Navi Mumbai, Dombivli, Kalyan, Nagpur, Nashik, and Pune. Social media management + Reels + viral content, Meta + Google ads, website + online booking + WhatsApp Cloud API integration, Google Business Profile optimisation + local SEO, and patient lead generation. We work with clinics that don't have in-house marketing teams — treating the marketing function as an outsourced growth partner, not a vendor. Every answer below reflects live clinic work.
    </div>

    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How to choose a marketing agency for a hair transplant clinic in Nashik?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Ten-point framework: (1) Named hair transplant / cosmetic surgery client work with verifiable case studies + graft-count-based attribution. (2) ASCI + MCI compliance + Drugs and Magic Remedies Act familiarity. (3) High-AOV surgical-decision funnel expertise (Rs 60,000-4 lakh procedures). (4) Medical-tourism catchment marketing (patients from Tier 2/3 + international come to Nashik for procedures). (5) GMB + local SEO for Nashik — Moderate GMB competition — 50-70 clinics ranked. College Road + Gangapur Road medical cluster. (6) WhatsApp Cloud API + inside-sales flow for surgical consultation. (7) Before-after 6-12 month growth documentation methodology. (8) Reels + long-form video production capacity (surgeon technique, patient journey). (9) Ad-spend transparency. (10) Contract 6-month MSA + cancellation + 100% client IP + patient data ownership.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a realistic monthly retainer for a hair transplant clinic in Nashik?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Retainer: Rs 28,000-1.8 lakh (typically upper half of range because hair transplant needs high-quality video + medical-tourism landing pages + inside-sales support). Starter (Rs 50-90K Nashik) for solo surgeon with Rs 10-30 lakh/month procedure revenue. Growth (Rs 1.2-2.5L Nashik) for 2-3 surgeon clinics Rs 30 lakh-1.5 crore/month revenue. Enterprise (Rs 2.5-4L+ Nashik) for chain or destination clinic Rs 1.5+ crore/month. Ad spend separate: Rs 30,000-2.8 lakh (often upper end because high CPL is offset by high AOV).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What compliance do marketing agencies need to know for hair transplant in Nashik?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Same medical-advertising base as dermatology + trichology. Hair-transplant-specific: cannot guarantee outcome (individual variation in graft-yield); before-after must include disclaimer + patient consent; surgeon-credential display must be accurate + verifiable; facility + team + technology claims must be truthful; medical-tourism marketing to Tier 2/3 + international must comply with home-country + destination-country advertising rules. In Nashik, Maharashtra Medical Council + Maharashtra FDA + NMC (Nashik Municipal Corporation) enforcement + surgical facility norms.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What named hair transplant client work should a marketing agency show?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Verifiable: (1) Live URLs of hair transplant clinic YouTube (long-form + surgeon technique) + Instagram + GMB, (2) 2-3 named references, (3) case studies with graft-count-weighted attribution + procedure revenue + medical-tourism catchment breakdown, (4) before-after video library samples (compliance-safe with consent + disclaimer). Red flag: no named hair-transplant work, or generic 'we do medical marketing' without hair-transplant-specific proof.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What contract terms + exit clauses should hair transplant clinics negotiate?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Same core: 6-month MSA + cancellation after month 3, ad-spend transparent pass-through, 100% client IP on creative + video library + booking + patient data. Hair-transplant-specific: because procedure AOV is Rs 60,000-4 lakh + medical-tourism patients travel, contract must cover before/during/post-procedure content workflow + patient consent management + long-tail before-after documentation over 6-12 months.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What team structure will a hair transplant marketing agency assign to a Nashik clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Growth-tier: Account Director + Performance marketer + Creative pod (video editor + Reels + long-form YouTube producer + designer, 8-15 pieces/month) + Social media manager + Content writer (medical-tourism landing pages + long-form + WhatsApp inside-sales scripts) + Local SEO + GMB specialist + Inside-sales advisor (high-AOV consultation conversion). Founder + senior on quarterly QBR.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What reporting cadence to expect from a hair transplant marketing agency?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Weekly: patient inquiries + cost per lead + cost per booked consultation + inside-sales conversion rate + GMB rank + video reach + WhatsApp inquiries. Monthly QBR: full P&amp;L + procedure-revenue attribution + graft-count-weighted + medical-tourism catchment + creative + channel review. Quarterly business review + long-cycle before-after content review. Compliance review monthly.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">In-house vs agency vs hybrid for a Nashik hair transplant clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">In-house at Rs 1.5 crore+/month procedure revenue. Full agency for Rs 10 lakh-1.5 crore/month (most hair transplant clinics). Hybrid at Rs 80 lakh-1.5 crore/month. In Nashik, most solo + 2-3 surgeon clinics operate best with full agency because video-heavy content + medical-tourism marketing + inside-sales expertise require specialist teams. ITD specifically serves clinics that don't have in-house marketing teams.</div>
      </div>
